 64, R4.8 -u ignored on line 66)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (existing differential tests covering R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1-R4.4, R5.2, R5.3 -- R4.5-R4.8 are not yet tested)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, NormalizeFunc API)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (full PRD -- confirm R4.5-R4.8 definitions and acceptance criteria)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for flag aliases -A, -e, -t, -u and update header comment\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R4.5: the -A flag is equivalent to -vET. Run cat -A on a file containing control characters (0x01, 0x02), tabs, and newlines. Verify stdout matches gcat -A byte-for-byte.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R4.6: the -e flag is equivalent to -vE. Run cat -e on a file containing control characters and newlines. Verify stdout matches gcat -e byte-for-byte. Tabs must pass through unchanged since -T is not activated by -e.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R4.7: the -t flag is equivalent to -vT. Run cat -t on a file containing control characters and tabs. Verify stdout matches gcat -t byte-for-byte. Line-end markers ($) must not appear since -E is not activated by -t.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R4.8: the -u flag is accepted but has no effect on output. Run cat -u on a file. Verify stdout matches gcat -u byte-for-byte, confirming identical passthrough.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Add differential test combining a flag alias with an independent flag: run cat -A -n on a file with control characters, tabs, blank lines, and newlines. Verify stdout matches gcat -A -n, confirming line numbering interacts correctly with the combined -vET behavior.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: 